# UC-001 · REST adapter

> Partial of `docs/use-cases/UC-001-create-user/`. Owner: `rest-api-architect`.
> Inherits the canonical names from `00-caso-de-uso.md` and the ports from `10-dominio.md` —
> doesn't reinvent them.
> Contains no code. Reference shapes in
> `.claude/skills/rest-api-architect/templates/`.
> Rules applied, never reproduced: `@.claude/rules/api-rest.md`.

| Field | Value |
|---|---|
| Parent spec | `00-caso-de-uso.md` |
| Domain partial | `10-dominio.md` |
| Resource | `users` |
| Version prefix | `/api/v1` |
| Divergences from `10-dominio.md` | none |

## 1 · Endpoints

One per line. `operationId` is a contract: it becomes a method name in the generated client.

| Method | Path | `operationId` | Inbound port | Success |
|---|---|---|---|---|
| `POST` | `/api/v1/users` | `createUser` | `CreateUserUseCase` | 201 + `Location` + representation |
| `GET` | `/api/v1/users` | `listUsers` | `ListUsersQuery` | 200 + page envelope |
| `GET` | `/api/v1/users/{userId}` | `getUser` | `ListUsersQuery.byId` | 200 + representation |

No `PUT` nor `PATCH` in this iteration: the parent spec has no update use case.
Adding an endpoint with no use case behind it is guessing the contract.

`POST /api/v1/users` requires `Idempotency-Key`: it creates a resource. The `GET`s don't — they're safe.

## 2 · DTOs

| DTO | Direction | Fields | Shape validation |
|---|---|---|---|
| `CreateUserRequest` | input | `email`, `name`, `departmentId?` | `@NotBlank` + `@Email` + `@Size(max=254)`; `name` `@NotBlank` + `@Size(max=120)` |
| `UserResponse` | output | `id`, `email`, `name`, `createdAt` | — |
| `PageResponse<UserResponse>` | output | `content`, `page{number,size,totalElements,totalPages}` | — |

Validation here is **shape** only. "Email already registered" isn't `@Email`: it's an
aggregate invariant, lives in `10-dominio.md`, and comes out as 422 — see block 3.

DTO ↔ domain translation in `UserMapper`, static methods, manual. The DTO's `String`
becomes `Email` in the mapper and nowhere else.

## 3 · Error map

Each exception from `10-dominio.md`, its status, and the `errorCode` the client sees. This
table is the source of block 5 — no test case comes from anywhere but here.

| Situation | Domain exception | Status | `errorCode` | Extra fields |
|---|---|---|---|---|
| Email already registered | `BusinessRuleViolationException` | 422 | `EMAIL_ALREADY_REGISTERED` | `errorCode` |
| Given department doesn't exist | `NotFoundException` | 404 | `DEPARTMENT_NOT_FOUND` | `errorCode` |
| Unknown `userId` in `GET` | `NotFoundException` | 404 | `USER_NOT_FOUND` | `errorCode` |
| `Idempotency-Key` missing or malformed | `ValidationException` | 400 | `IDEMPOTENCY_KEY_INVALID` | `errorCode` |
| Same key, different body | `ConflictException` | 409 | `IDEMPOTENCY_KEY_REUSED` | `errorCode` |
| Required field missing, malformed `email` | — (bean validation) | 400 | **none** | `violations` |
| Unreadable JSON, incompatible type | — (deserialization) | 400 | **none** | — |
| Unmapped | — | 500 | **none** | `traceId` |

Bean validation never carries `errorCode`: it's structural, not from the domain.
`traceId` comes from Micrometer Tracing, `Tracer` injected into `ApiExceptionHandler`.

## 4 · Pagination, idempotency, and dependencies

**Pagination** — `GET /api/v1/users` is offset: `page` (0-based), `size` defaulting to 20
and capped at 100, `sort` defaulting to `createdAt,desc`. Tiebreak by `id` is mandatory,
added in the application and not requested from the client. Cursor isn't used here: the
expected volume (200,000 rows, from `20-persistencia.md`) doesn't justify it.

**Idempotency** — two halves, and only the first belongs to this partial:

| Half | Where it lives | In this partial |
|---|---|---|
| Header presence and format | `IdempotencyKeyInterceptor` in the adapter | yes — 400 above |
| Recording the key + the effect, in the same transaction | application layer | no — only declared as needed |
| `idempotency_keys` table (route, caller, body hash, status, body, TTL >= 24 h) | `20-persistencia.md` | no — **handed off to `persistence-architect`** |

**Dependencies to add** — the executor applies them to `pom.xml`; this skill only
declares them.

| Artifact | Why | Version |
|---|---|---|
| `org.springdoc:springdoc-openapi-starter-webmvc-ui` | Generates `openapi.json` from the code | **not managed by the Spring Boot BOM** — resolve at runtime, never from memory |
| `io.micrometer:micrometer-tracing-bridge-otel` | Source of `traceId` | managed by the BOM |
| `spring-boot-starter-validation` | Bean validation on the DTOs | managed by the BOM |

## 5 · Contract test cases

What the test has to assert. **The test code comes from the executor**, not this skill.
Asserting only the status number isn't enough: a wrong `errorCode` would slip through.

| Case | Request | Asserts |
|---|---|---|
| Happy creation | valid `POST` + key | 201, `Location` header present, `email` in the body |
| Business rule | `POST` with an already-registered email | 422 **and** `errorCode = EMAIL_ALREADY_REGISTERED` |
| Invalid shape | `POST` without `email` | 400, `violations[0].field = email`, `errorCode` absent |
| Missing key | `POST` without `Idempotency-Key` | 400 |
| Idempotency | two identical `POST`s with the same key | only one user created, two identical responses, same status |
| Reused key | same key, different body | 409 **and** `errorCode = IDEMPOTENCY_KEY_REUSED` |
| Empty page | `GET` with no results | 200 with `content: []` — never 204 |
| Stable ordering | `GET` page 0 and page 1 | empty intersection |
| `size` above the maximum | `GET ?size=500` | 400 — never truncated silently |

Body-shape fixtures: `templates/error-responses.json.example` and
`templates/page-response.json.example`.
